{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1540313808,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNzMxMDA3NDE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2939","origin":"github"},"title":"'add -d. .' shows confusing error on a moved file","message":"[ +cc @AdinaWagner, who ran into this ]\n\nWhen trying to add a moved file, `datalad add -d. .` spits out an error, although the resulting commit seems fine.  The `-d.`  is required to trigger the issue because otherwise `AnnotatedPaths` is called with `modified=None` and the problematic [`get_modified_subpaths` call][0] is avoided.\n\nI haven't dug any deeper or thought about possible fixes.  I suppose this issue is resolved with datalad-revolution, so it may not be worth fixing in the meantime.\n\n```sh\nset -x\n\ndatalad create add-moved\ncd add-moved\ntouch foo \u0026\u0026 datalad add foo\ngit tag base\n\n# Works fine when a dataset isn't specified\nmv foo foo_moved \u0026\u0026 datalad add .\n# add(ok): /tmp/add-moved/foo_moved (file)\n# add(ok): /tmp/add-moved (dataset)\n# save(ok): /tmp/add-moved (dataset)\n# action summary:\n#   add (ok: 2)\n#   save (ok: 1)\n\n# Fails if a dataset is specified\ngit reset --hard base\nmv foo foo_moved \u0026\u0026 datalad add -d. .\n# [WARNING] Running add resulted in stderr output: git-annex: /tmp/add-moved/foo not found\n# git-annex: add: 1 failed\n#\n# add(ok): foo_moved (file)\n# [ERROR  ] not found [add(/tmp/add-moved/foo)]\n# add(error): foo (file) [not found]\n# save(ok): /tmp/add-moved (dataset)\n# action summary:\n#   add (error: 1, ok: 1)\n#   save (ok: 1)\n\n# Commit was create, though\ngit diff HEAD^-\n# diff --git a/foo b/foo_moved\n# similarity index 100%\n# rename from foo\n# rename to foo_moved\n```\n\n[0]: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/dd3ccd6c18e5d1372e6c490881ca35e3af4a8fe3/datalad/interface/annotate_paths.py#L556","files":null}]}